        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The Annales school (named for its journal, Annales d'histoire économique et sociale, founded\n1929) transformed historical practice in the 20th century more than any other single movement.\nIt challenged narrative political history with structural, interdisciplinary, long-term analysis.\nIts four generations each took the project in new directions."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md#003",
      "path": [
        "01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:social-history:01-annales-school, git-history:social-history:01-annales-school]",
        "canonical_path": "social-history/01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md",
        "concepts": "[annales, school]",
        "current_path": "social-history/01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md",
        "id": "maxim:social-history:annales-school",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "social-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[annales, school]",
        "section": "social-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Annales School and Total History",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                   THE ANNALES SCHOOL                              |\n|                                                                   |\n|  GENERATION 1 (1929-1945)     GENERATION 2 (1945-1968)            |\n|   ---------------------        ---------------------------        |\n|    BLOCH and FEBVRE             BRAUDEL                           |\n|    Founders (Strasbourg         Longue duree                      |\n|    then Paris)                  Med. World / Phil. II             |\n|    Anti-political,              Structures, conjunctures,         |\n|    anti-narrative               events                            |\n|    Geographic/social                                              |\n|    history                                                        |\n|   ---------------------        ---------------------------        |\n|                                                                   |\n|  GENERATION 3 (1968-1989)     GENERATION 4 (1989-)                |\n|   ---------------------        ---------------------------        |\n|    LE ROY LADURIE,              Cultural/micro turn               |\n|    DUBY, LE GOFF                Chartier, Revel                   |\n|    Serial / quantitative        Back toward narrative             |\n|    Mentalities                  Microhistory                      |\n|    Economic & social            New cultural history              |\n|   ---------------------        ---------------------------        |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
