      "text": "### Marc Bloch (1886-1944)"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md#007",
      "path": [
        "01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:social-history:01-annales-school, git-history:social-history:01-annales-school]",
        "canonical_path": "social-history/01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md",
        "concepts": "[annales, school]",
        "current_path": "social-history/01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md",
        "id": "maxim:social-history:annales-school",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "social-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[annales, school]",
        "section": "social-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Annales School and Total History",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  KEY WORKS:\n  Feudal Society (1939-40): systematic analysis of medieval European society.\n  Not a narrative but structural: how did feudalism work as a social system?"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md#008",
      "path": [
        "01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:social-history:01-annales-school, git-history:social-history:01-annales-school]",
        "canonical_path": "social-history/01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md",
        "concepts": "[annales, school]",
        "current_path": "social-history/01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md",
        "id": "maxim:social-history:annales-school",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "social-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[annales, school]",
        "section": "social-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Annales School and Total History",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "COMPARATIVE METHOD:\n  Bloch advocated comparison across regions and periods.\n  \"To understand France, compare it with England.\"\n  Method: identify similar phenomena in different contexts to isolate causes."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md#009",
      "path": [
        "01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:social-history:01-annales-school, git-history:social-history:01-annales-school]",
        "canonical_path": "social-history/01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md",
        "concepts": "[annales, school]",
        "current_path": "social-history/01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md",
        "id": "maxim:social-history:annales-school",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "social-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[annales, school]",
        "section": "social-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Annales School and Total History",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THE HISTORIAN'S CRAFT (written in hiding; incomplete at his death):\n  Methodological testament.\n  \"What is history for? What does the historian do?\"\n  \"For a long time, history was understood as the science of the past. This\n  is an absurd formula. How could the past, as such, be an object of science?\"\n  History is the science of human societies in time."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md#010",
      "path": [
        "01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:social-history:01-annales-school, git-history:social-history:01-annales-school]",
        "canonical_path": "social-history/01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md",
        "concepts": "[annales, school]",
        "current_path": "social-history/01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md",
        "id": "maxim:social-history:annales-school",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "social-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[annales, school]",
        "section": "social-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Annales School and Total History",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DEATH:\n  Bloch was a French Jew who joined the Resistance.\n  He was captured by the Gestapo and executed in 1944.\n  His death became symbolic of the stakes of historical commitment.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md#011",
      "path": [
        "01-ANNALES-SCHOOL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
